        "original_id": "8e5f39cc-c0f8-56a1-bc60-b0b121148081",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, NASCAR Grand National races\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia, Middle Georgia Raceway\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series sponsorship, race naming, race scheduling\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1966 and 1971, Middle Georgia Raceway hosted nine NASCAR Grand National races, a series now known as the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series.\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, the former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named the race after the winner of an essay contest held during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two annual Cup Series races at Richmond Raceway, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring as the first race.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
